          "question": "q-42988",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/state.json",
